      "body": "## Overview\n\nWith the V2 model runner, models whose attention is encoder-only (non-causal, no KV cache) produce wrong outputs when they\nare served with `cudagraph_mode=FULL`.\n\nA FULL CUDA graph for mixed batches is captured on a dummy batch that spreads its tokens over many requests (down to one\ntoken each), but it may later replay a batch with one long prompt. `DefaultModelState` already builds the captured\nattention metadata from the batch's promised `max_query_len` for this reason. `EncoderOnlyModelState` instead used the\ndummy batch's actual largest query length, so the encoder attention kernels in the graph kept a very short\n`max_seqlen_q` / `max_seqlen_k`. Prompts that replay such a graph are then computed incorrectly. There is no error.\n\nThe fix applies the same rule as `DefaultModelState`: use `input_batch.max_query_len` when the batch sets it, and fall\nback to the largest scheduled query length otherwise.\n\n```python\nmax_query_len = input_batch.max_query_len\nif max_query_len is None:\n    max_query_len = int(input_batch.num_scheduled_tokens.max())\n```\n\nOne file changed (`vllm/v1/worker/gpu/model_states/encoder_only.py`), plus a regression test.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Encoder-only models served with `cudagraph_mode=FULL` give the same outputs as eager execution.\n- No change for `PIECEWISE` or `NONE`, for decoder models, or for batches without FULL graphs.\n- With the fix, FULL graphs are a correct option for these models: slightly faster single-request reads than PIECEWISE,\n  about equal under load (table below).\n\n## Validation\n\n| test | hardware | main | this PR |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `tests/v1/cudagraph/test_encoder_only_full_cudagraph.py`: `hmellor/tiny-random-LlamaForCausalLM` with `is_causal=False`, FP32, prompts of 23 / 150 / 600 / 1000 tokens one at a time; FULL (capture to 1024) vs eager, last-position logprobs, atol = rtol = 1e-4 | L40S | **fails** (max abs difference 0.034) | passes |\n| 8B non-causal decoder fine-tune, FP8, accuracy eval of 13,904 requests, FULL graphs (capture to 8192) vs PIECEWISE | GB200 | 1.5-2 points lower than PIECEWISE (wrong reads) | **identical to PIECEWISE**, two full repeats on each of three configurations (capture to 8192, capture to 2048, 0.6 memory utilization) |\n| same eval | L40S | pending | pending |\n| ruff check / format | — | | clean |\n\n## Benchmark\n\nNVIDIA GB200 (one GPU), 8B non-causal decoder fine-tune, FP8, `max_cudagraph_capture_size=8192`, one exclusive node,\neach configuration measured alone.\n\n| | FULL, this PR | PIECEWISE |\n|---|---|---|\n| 512-token read, concurrency 1, p50 / p95 | 13.4 / 14.8 ms | 14.0 / 16.5 ms |\n| mixed prompts (~1.7k tokens), concurrency 1, requests/s | 35.3 | 32.7 |\n| same, concurrency 16, requests/s | 41.8 | 42.8 |\n| same, concurrency 64, requests/s | 41.1 | 42.3 |\n\nThe main point of the PR is correctness: on main, FULL looks faster (12.6 ms for the same 512-token read) only because\nit computes the wrong attention.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
